.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-DELETE-CERTIFICATE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-delete-certificate \- delete a certificate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm delete-certificate
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a certificate and its private key, immediately and without a
grace period.
.PP
Unlike
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1),
there is nothing to lose by acting at once: no data becomes
unreadable. An API gateway listener already serving the certificate
keeps the copy it loaded until it is restarted, and generates a new
self-signed one if it restarts and finds none \- so a listener is never
left with nothing to answer with, though its callers will be shown a
certificate nobody has vouched for until a real one is imported under
the same name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Certificate name, within the caller's own account and namespace.
Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The certificate was deleted; its name and ERN are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
No certificate of that name exists, the server could not be reached, or
it rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint https://localhost:5566 ekm delete-certificate \e
    --name eag-development
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-certificate (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-import-certificate (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-certificates (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-get-certificate (1)
